  "question": {
    ":question/id": "096f10be-0279-55c5-9454-8491724a735c",
    ":question/problem": "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,8=2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -16 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-16=2\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -16 \\\\ 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,8=2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -16 \\\\ 8 & -16\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-16=2\\cdot (-8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -16 \\\\ 8 & -16\\end{bmatrix}.$",
